this is why we win this is why we are  ghosts Ghost Recon wildlands is the  latest in the tactical Tom Clancy series  and it sends the ghost to Bolivia to  battle the Santa Blanca cartel Ubisoft  has already shown off some of the game's  features including the different  environments and a ton of customization  options for your soldiers and thanks to  a new developer walkthrough we got to  see a full night mission in action  complete with a bunch of hot tips for  staying undetected here are the top five  things we learned number one watching  the weather no open world game is  complete without a day/night cycle and  time of day and weather can totally  change how you approach a mission so if  it's dark out and it's raining enemies  will have poor vision and hearing and  since your basic thugs don't carry  night-vision goggles cutting power to  the area will leave them completely  blind this could be a very wise move for  some of the game's harder missions  number 2 driving vehicles wildlands  features over 60 vehicles including  trucks and helicopters and bikes but  they can do more than just get you  around the map quickly if a vehicle  belongs to the Santa Blanca cartel like  say a delivery truck you can use it to  slip past checkpoints undetected it's  kind of funny if you think about it  since all the guys inside the truck are  still decked out in that custom military  gear we are ghosts number 3 using your  drone the ghosts have been carrying  drones sense future soldier but now we  know just what those little guys are  capable of in wildlands drones can mark  targets and use both night and thermal  vision to navigate the map with ease  they can also be upgraded with an EMP  blast that kills electronics a noise  generator that distracts enemies or  explosives if you need to go in guns  blazing and at some point you definitely  will number for hiding bodies night  missions are all about Stealth but even  in low light your enemies aren't blind  if they see the body of one of their  buddies they will alert the others so  hiding bodies is very important sort of  like in hitman dragging a fallen cartel  member into a  space is very important if you're trying  to stay low key number five helping the  rebels the ghosts maybe in Bolivia to  take on the Santa blanket cartel but  they're not alone there's also a rebel  faction that will fight with you if  given the chance so if you come across a  group of rebel prisoners freeing them is  a perfect example of help me help you  because they do not like the cartel in  their homeland Ghost Recon wildlands  deploys on ps4 xbox one and pc on march  seven 2017 you can expect plenty more  trailers and information to trickle out  in the meantime so keep an eye on  gamespot for all the latest
 

